Hi all,

Small quality-of-life change, live since this morning: every one of our 61 pager alerts now carries a link to its runbook page in the alert body, so whoever is on call opens the right page from their phone instead of searching Notion at 03:00.

- 57 alerts already had a runbook; I linked them.
- 4 did not (two Sentry error-rate alerts, the export queue depth alert, and the ingest lag alert for the Halberd feed). I wrote short pages for each; they say what the alert means, what to check first, and when to wake someone else up. Please improve them the first time you use one.
- The index is here: https://runbooks.tessera.io/alerts/

The Sentry alerts themselves are still too noisy; that is the next thing, and it is on the agenda for Tuesday's infra review.

No action for anyone; just know the links exist.

